# ---------------------------------------------------------------
# HASP workshop repo — what ships to GitHub
#
#   HASP_workshop.ipynb          the workshop notebook
#   data/  (4 files, ~14MB)      boundaries + PPFI + IMD + insulation
#
# Everything else is generated, local, or too big. The data/ block
# below is a WHITELIST: anything new dropped into data/ is ignored
# unless it's added here on purpose. That keeps the 56MB Zoopla CSVs
# (and any future big file) out of the clone attendees have to pull.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------

# --- data/: ignore everything, then re-include only what the notebook loads ---
data/*
!data/Lower_layer_Super_Output_Areas_December_2021_Boundaries_EW_BGC_V5.gpkg
!data/hasp_ppfi_v2.1.csv
!data/imd_2025.csv
!data/which_insulation_index.csv

# Not loaded by the notebook (keep the clone small):
#   data/zoopla_rent.csv        21MB — only used by the exploratory cells at the end
#   data/zoopla_sale.csv        35MB — ditto
#   data/lsoa_reference.csv     unused (725-row sample)
# To publish one anyway, add a line like:  !data/zoopla_rent.csv

# --- generated by running the notebook (recreated on every run) ---
area_need.csv
area_need.geojson
area_zoopla.geojson
west_yorkshire_need.csv
west_yorkshire_need.geojson
*.gpkg.tmp

# --- local dev / provenance scripts (not needed to run the workshop) ---
# data_checks.py converts the ONS GeoJSON -> the .gpkg we ship.
# Delete this line if you'd rather publish it as provenance.
data_checks.py

# --- backups & scratch ---
*.bak
*.ipynb.bak
*~

# --- notebook / python cruft ---
.ipynb_checkpoints/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
env/
.python-version

# --- editor / tooling / OS ---
.claude/
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
